# Files that belong in the repository but should never be served to the public.
#
# The site is static, so Vercel publishes every file it deploys. Without this,
# https://casttco.online/supabase/migrations/0003_consultation_slots.sql
# returned 200 and handed anyone the complete schema: table names, column
# names and the row level security policies protecting them.
#
# None of it grants access -- RLS is enforced whether or not an attacker knows
# it exists -- but publishing the schema tells them exactly what is protected
# and where to look for something that is not.

# Database schema and migrations.
supabase/

# The pre-commit secret scanner, which otherwise publishes the patterns it
# looks for -- a useful hint to anyone wanting to sneak a key past it.
.githooks/

# Documents the names of the environment variables. Harmless, but there is no
# reason for it to be reachable over the web.
.env.example

# Local git metadata, in case it is ever present in a build context.
.git/
